wildos-mail (0.2.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Calendar is a tab of Mail's window; Open in new window on the rail.
  * Gmail accounts bring their calendar.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 23:10:00 +0000

wildos-mail (0.2.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Calendar (wildos-calendar), on evolution-data-server's calendar service:
    day, work week, week and month, events with people, repeats, reminders
    and notes, Google, iCloud, CalDAV and web calendars, and reminders shown
    as notifications from sign-in.
  * Mail answers invitations: Accept, Maybe and Decline, with the day the
    event is on beside them.
  * Mail and Calendar share the app rail.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 22:20:00 +0000

wildos-mail (0.1.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Camel's IMAP and SMTP modules come from evolution-data-server-camel-providers,
    split out of Wild OS's rebuild of evolution-data-server, instead of copies
    carried by Mail, so they get Debian's fixes.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 21:10:00 +0000

wildos-mail (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

